# iOS Home Grid — a 4x6 grid of gradient app icons; tapping one measures it
# on the UI thread and expands it into a full-screen detail (custom
# shared-element-like transition over a native stack); the detail is dismissed
# by dragging it down past 300pt (it scales down with friction and the icon
# springs back into place) or by its X button.
# What this test covers: opening icons from different rows/columns, the
# drag-to-dismiss path, a short drag released below the threshold (scale
# springs back, detail stays), a slow long drag, tapping a second icon while
# the first transition is still running, and repeated open/close cycles.
# The detail's own X (top-right, under the debug-only dev-menu gear in this
# build) is not tapped: the gear catches the touch in Debug.
# Grid: x 54/152/250/348, rows y 110/208/306/404/502/600.
context platform=ios
open "demos://animations/ios-home-grid"
wait 2000
wait "label=\"Close\"" 30000
wait 1500
# Open, dismiss by dragging down fast past the threshold.
press 152 208
wait 1500
gesture pan 200 300 0 420 350
wait 1500
# Another icon; short drag (springs back), then the real dismiss.
press 250 306
wait 1500
gesture pan 200 300 0 150 500
wait 1200
gesture pan 200 250 0 450 300
wait 1500
# Bottom row, last column.
press 348 600
wait 1500
# Slow long drag.
gesture pan 200 250 0 450 1500
wait 1500
# First column, middle row.
press 54 404
wait 1500
gesture pan 200 300 0 420 350
wait 1500
# Tap a second icon while the first transition is still running.
press 152 502
wait 150
press 250 502
wait 1500
gesture pan 200 300 0 420 350
wait 1500
# Quick open/close cycles.
press 348 404
wait 900
gesture pan 200 300 0 420 300
wait 900
press 54 600
wait 900
gesture pan 200 300 0 420 300
wait 1500
wait "label=\"Close\"" 15000
press "role=\"button\" label=\"Close\""
wait 1500
